---
name: decide_context
description: >
  The always-on context block appended to a live decide observation (issue
  #580): the sim clock time, the plan's current stop, and how long the agent
  has been on that stop. Rendered by cognition.decide_context_block() only
  when the step loop threads a SimClock (the bake and the offline tests pass
  none). The deterministic mock brain reads only the observation's first
  line, so this block can never change a mock decision. The numbers are
  computed in Python (they are data, not text); only the wording lives here.
inputs:
  time:
    type: string
    description: In-game wall-clock time, e.g. "Monday 12:05 PM".
  place:
    type: string
    description: The current stop's place, e.g. "Houston Hall".
  activity:
    type: string
    description: The current stop's activity, e.g. "eating lunch".
  minutes:
    type: integer
    description: >
      The stop's intended duration in minutes. Optional; the planned clause
      is dropped when unset (the schedule says stay indefinitely) or 0.
  elapsed:
    type: integer
    description: >
      Minutes the agent has been on this stop so far (walking toward it
      counts). The sentence is dropped at 0 -- the stop just began.
sample:
  time: Monday 12:05 PM
  place: Houston Hall
  activity: eating lunch
  minutes: 40
  elapsed: 15
---
Right now it is {{ time }}.
Your plan's current stop: {{ activity }} at {{ place }}{% if minutes %} (planned ~{{ minutes }} min){% endif %}.{% if elapsed %} You have been on this stop for {{ elapsed }} min.{% endif %}
